# Line endings a fresh clone gets, on any operating system.
#
# A shell script with CRLF line endings dies on Linux and macOS. The kernel
# reads the carriage return as part of the interpreter path on the first
# line and reports "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M: no such file or directory".
# The same script still runs when a shell is called on it by hand, so the
# fault appears only on the machine that clones the repo.
#
# The files only Windows runs keep CRLF. Everything else is left to git's
# own default, so no file already committed changes shape.

*.sh text eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

*.ttf binary
*.ttc binary
